      "role": "user",
      "content": "Yeah, exactly. I don't want it to feel like a modern person writing about the past; it needs to feel lived-in. I'm thinking of a scene where a white sheriff pulls over a Black man who happens to be a respected community leader—maybe a preacher or a teacher. The sheriff is feeling threatened by this man's influence in the town. Can you help me draft some of the dialogue the sheriff might use to try and intimidate him? I want the language to be period-accurate to show how much disrespect there was.",
